Summary: ntdll: is_apple_silicon(), whether the process runs under Rosetta 2, for other patches
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 18947
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Changes: only is_apple_silicon() from CW HACK 18947, verbatim, in its own
    #ifdef __APPLE__ block
Upstream: no
Why: Adds a static helper to dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c that asks
 sysctl.proc_translated once whether the process runs translated by
 Rosetta 2. CrossOver defines it with CW HACK 18947
 (ntdll-rosetta-cross-process-code-writes), and
 ntdll-rosetta-refuse-ldt-entries calls it too. Kept in a patch of its own
 so either can be dropped without breaking the other. It changes nothing
 by itself.
Programs: none known
Status: 2026-11-26: split out of ntdll-rosetta-cross-process-code-writes;
 the patched source is the same apart from an #endif/#ifdef pair between
 the two blocks. Not yet in a build.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6671,6 +6671,27 @@
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+static int is_apple_silicon(void)
+{
+    static int apple_silicon_status, did_check = 0;
+    if (!did_check)
+    {
+        /* returns 0 for native process or on error, 1 for translated */
+        int ret = 0;
+        size_t size = sizeof(ret);
+        if (sysctlbyname( "sysctl.proc_translated", &ret, &size, NULL, 0 ) == -1)
+            apple_silicon_status = 0;
+        else
+            apple_silicon_status = ret;
+
+        did_check = 1;
+    }
+
+    return apple_silicon_status;
+}
+#endif
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *             NtWriteVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
  *             ZwWriteVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
